; TORRE HUNDIDA - first-person view tiles (games/dungeon GDD 2.3, 7.1). Generated by the
; pixel-artist's script, then the source of truth. Pieces that use them: res/view.pcs.
; BG tiles cannot be flipped: right-side pieces have their own tiles.
; One corridor: every wall face has 4 stone courses whose lines follow the perspective
; (side-wall lines meet the front courses at the corners: y 32/48/63 at P1, 36/48/59 at P2,
; 40/48/56 at P3); ceiling joints and floor ribs sit on the depth planes (y 16/24 and 80/72/64).
; Shading by distance: S0+F1 light + white lips, F2 50% dither + black mortar, S2/F3 dark +
; black, darkness black (tile DARK = 0). Vertical corners in the mortar colour, top/bottom black.
; BG rows (2 alternating tiles, even column first): 0-1 CEIL_NEAR, 2 CEIL_MID, 3 CEIL_FAR,
; 4-7 DARK, 8 FLOOR_FAR, 9 FLOOR_MID, 10 FLOOR_A FLOOR_B, 11 FLOOR_C FLOOR_D.
; <PIECE>_0 labels only mark where each piece's new tiles start (pieces share tiles).
